  "problemStatement": "Isolate the per-step residue law E(N) = E(⌈N/4⌉) + δ(N mod 8) of the non-three-square density error as a reusable lemma; establish the per-step bounds/residue dictionary of δ; and determine why the sustainable extremal descent rate is 4 (residue 6) rather than 5 (residue 7), given a single step can cost 5.",
  "knowledge": {
    "insights": [
      "The per-step error contribution δ is a function of N mod 8 only: δ(r) = ⌊(r+3)/4⌋ − r, values 0,0,−1,−2,−3,−3,−4,−5; this gives BOTH the one-sided sign (all ≤ 0) and the worst case.",
      "KEY: the maximal cost δ = −5 occurs only at residue 7, and N ≡ 7 (mod 8) forces ⌈N/4⌉ = (N+3)/4 = 2q+2 to be EVEN, so residue 7 cannot chain to itself. A −5 step is structurally isolated and cannot sustain.",
      "Residue 6 (cost 4) DOES chain to itself (when N/8 ≡ 2 mod 4), the mechanism of the parent's extremal family. So the sustainable extremal RATE is 4, not 5.",
      "OPEN sub-finding: the exact Θ(log N) leading constant is NOT simply 4 — cost-5 steps, though isolated, contribute O(1) bursts; pinning the constant requires counting residue-7 occurrences along a descent. The residue transition depends on higher bits (q mod 4), making it an automata-style optimization, genuinely harder than the parent's framing suggests."
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "delta: per-step error contribution function in Proofs/LagrangeFourSquaresWaringG2OQ03OQ05OQ01OQ01.lean",
      "error_step: per-step law E(N) = E(⌈N/4⌉) + delta (N mod 8) for all N",
      "delta_nonpos, neg_five_le_delta, delta_eq_{zero,neg_four,neg_five}_iff: bounds + residue dictionary",
      "quot_even_of_mod_seven, mod6_chains: the sustainability obstruction and its companion",
      "gap_step_le, gap_nonneg_and_step: per-step descent inequality"
    ],
